ets remain confident in Shaheen, supporting a Likely D rating with a mid-single-digit expected margin.", "watch": "Any additional polling showing DiLorenzo within a few points, or a favorable national environment for Republicans, could move this toward Lean D.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: Chris Pappas (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Chris Pappas is leaving the seat to run for Senate, making this an open contest in a district with only a slight Democratic lean. Stefany Shaheen, daughter of the former senator, survived a tight primary and enters the general with a large cash-on-hand edge and substantial super PAC support. Anthony DiLorenzo has raised competitively but has less money banked.\n\nRaters mostly call the race Likely Democratic, though a few say Lean Democratic. The one recent University of New Hampshire poll shows Shaheen up four, narrower than fundamentals alone would suggest, while prediction markets price her win probability above ninety percent. The forecast lands on a Likely Democratic hold with a mid-single-digit margin and meaningful uncertainty.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.937, "margin": 10.01}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9238, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9245, "margin": 9.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8928, "margin": 7.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.8695, "margin": 7.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.844, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.871, "margin": 7.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.8487, "margin": 6.0}]}